  'Currently thinking in the sun',
  'Powered by black coffee and Gregorian chants',
  'My Eagle Scout project had a fire ring. Yours?',
  'I peaked in marching band and I\u2019m okay with that',
  'SELECT * FROM life WHERE passion IS NOT NULL',
  'Ducky, Goose, and Eevee send their regards',
  'Two cats, one dog, zero regrets',
  'Ask me about my $68M AI solution',
  'The data doesn\u2019t lie, but it does need a good pipeline',
  'One man\u2019s side project is another man\u2019s portfolio',
  'GCP by day, disc golf by golden hour',
  'I wrote my first Python loop in high school. Never stopped.',
  'Pixel fonts are a personality trait',
  'Living proof that you can love both math and musicals',
  'Jafar in Aladdin, Von Hussler in Mary Poppins, Data Engineer in real life',
  'I built a self-driving car in college. The website was harder.',
  'Hot take: dbt is beautiful',
  'Somewhere between a spreadsheet and a sermon',
  'Husband, engineer, and occasional choir singer',
  'My resume has bullet points. My life has chapters.',
  'Making BigQuery do things it wasn\u2019t designed to do',
  'Prompt engineering is just talking to robots politely',
  '4.0 GPA in grad school and still learning every day',
  'The best code is the code you don\u2019t have to debug',
  'Automating myself out of a job, one script at a time',
  'Data pipelines are just plumbing for nerds',
  'I think in SQL and dream in Python',
  'Penn State made me. Ford sharpened me.',
  'Still chasing that perfect disc golf round',
  'Every dataset tells a story if you listen',
  'Running models on my laptop like it\u2019s 2026. Oh wait.',
  'The Quads taught me rhythm. Data taught me patience.',
  'Boy Scout values, engineer precision',
  'You can take the kid out of Pittsburgh, but not the yinzer out of the kid',
  'Airflow DAGs are just really organized to-do lists',
  'I once taught Python to middle schoolers. They taught me humility.',
  'Cloud infrastructure and campfire rings',
  'Vertex AI whisperer',
  'My wife married a data nerd and she\u2019s thriving',
  'Electivire is the GOAT and I will not be taking questions',
  'I read AnimData.xml files for fun',
  'Dog dad to a red fox lab named after a Pok\u00e9mon',
  'Built different (literally, I build data products)',
  'Gregorian chants are elite focus music',
  'From tearing down sheds to tearing through datasets',
  'Catholic Lofi is a real artist and you should listen',
  'RA by night, intern by day, student always',
  'I\u2019ve saved more money for Ford than I\u2019ll ever make',
  'One of 2 students picked from 250. Still grateful.',
  'The sun, a disc, and an open field. That\u2019s the dream.',
  'WPIALs in track, states in indoor, SQL in production',
  'Ship it and iterate',
  'Agentic workflows are the future. I\u2019m just early.',
  'I have strong opinions about data modeling',
  'My Galaxy Book runs LLMs. Your move.',
  'Passionate about things most people don\u2019t know exist',
  'Turning coffee into queries since 2019',
  'Best External Use of Data (2023). Best internal use: daily.',
  'Penn State Outdoor Club taught me to carry my own weight',
  'I sing in the choir and optimize in the cloud',
  'Ordinary man, extraordinary data',
  'Camping, coding, and competitive Pok\u00e9mon',
];

const tagline = taglines[Math.floor(Math.random() * taglines.length)];
---

<Layout title="Adam Kenawell" description="Personal website of Adam Kenawell — Data Engineer at Ford. Blog, projects, resume, and more.">
  <div class="page">
    <Header showNav={false} />

    <main>
      <p class="tagline" id="tagline">{tagline}</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {cards.map((card) => (
          <a class="card" href={card.href}>
            <span>{card.title}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>

<script define:vars={{ taglines }}>
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    const el = document.getElementById('tagline');
    if (el) {
      el.textContent = taglines[Math.floor(Math.random() * taglines.length)];
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  main {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .tagline {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .cards {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .card {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 200px;
    height: 200px;
    border: 2px solid rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.5);
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    transition: background-color 0.2s, color 0.2s, transform 0.2s, border-color 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
  }

  .card:hover {
    background-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--accent);
    transform: translateY(-4px) scale(1.05);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.35), 0 4px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3), 0 0 20px rgba(var(--accent-rgb), 0.15);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    main {
      gap: 1.25rem;
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }

    .card {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 280px;
      height: 80px;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
